    "method": "Area means inside a circular radius around each coordinate. NASADEM elevation and pixel-level slope use 30 m data from February 2000, not the selected year; coverage is approximately 56\u00b0S\u201360\u00b0N. MODIS shortwave white-sky albedo uses MCD43A3 at 500 m with mandatory QA bit 0 = 0 and values in [0,1]. Its daily images use overlapping 16-day windows. MOD11A2 day and night land surface temperatures use 1 km 8-day composites with mandatory QA bits 0\u20131 = 0. MODIS images are averaged by pixel across the selected calendar year, then spatially averaged; day and night are independently masked, so their difference is the difference of separate means, not a paired daily swing. LST is surface temperature, not air temperature or thermal inertia. Missing or masked coverage is null. The site coordinates may themselves be placeholders."
